# API

The API is a NestJS app (`apps/api/src/main.ts`, `apps/api/src/app.module.ts`). Feature modules own controller + service (+ optional zod DTO). Handlers create metadata, enqueue jobs, and return IDs. They do not run transcription, summarization, KB sync, hook generation, or FFmpeg.

```ts
// ❌ BAD
@Post(':id/transcribe')
async transcribe(@Param('id') id: string) {
  return this.speech.transcribe(input);
}

// ✅ GOOD
@Post()
async create(@Body(new ZodValidationPipe(createRecordingRequestSchema)) body: CreateRecordingRequest) {
  const recording = await this.recordings.create(body);
  await this.queue.enqueue({ name: 'ingest-video', payload: { recordingId: recording.id } });
  return { id: recording.id };
}
```

## Validation

Use `@mintreels/schema` zod schemas as DTOs via `ZodValidationPipe`. Do not add class-validator DTOs. Add a feature `*.dto.ts` only when the HTTP request shape differs from `*InsertSchema`.

Import status, filter, accent, ratio, and env-key **enums** from `@mintreels/schema`. Do not hardcode `'ready'`, `'failed'`, `'mint'`, or `'AI_PROVIDER'` in handlers.

## Reads

Controllers stay thin. Services call repository `find` / `findOne` / `count`. Do not add QueryBuilder in `apps/api`.

A repository is **one table**. If a feature needs recordings + clips + jobs, the **service** calls `RecordingRepository`, `ClipRepository`, and `JobRepository` and combines the results. Do not put multi-table orchestration on a repository.

## Route surface

- `POST/GET /api/recordings`, `GET/DELETE /api/recordings/:id`
- `GET /api/recordings/:id/processing`, `POST /api/recordings/:id/retry`
- `GET /api/recordings/:id/transcript`, `GET /api/recordings/:id/transcript.vtt`
- `GET/POST /api/recordings/:id/summary`
- `POST /api/recordings/:id/add-to-global-kb`
- `GET /api/recordings/:id/hooks`, `POST /api/recordings/:id/hooks/generate`
- `POST /api/recordings/:id/hooks/:hookId/export`
- `POST /api/recordings/:id/moments/search` (sync embed + transcript-window search; no job)
- `POST /api/recordings/:id/moments/ask` (sync LLM route: transcript Q&A, clip search, or funny reject)
- `GET/POST /api/knowledge-bases`
- `GET /api/clips`, `GET /api/clips/filters`, `GET /api/clips/:id`
- `POST /api/clips` (owned recording time range; prompt search or arbitrary range)

Wire providers at the composition root (`providers/ProvidersModule`). Do not import PyAI or vendor SDKs in controllers or services.

## Swagger (mandatory for every controller)

Every controller **must** carry complete `@nestjs/swagger` decorators so FE developers have accurate docs at `/docs`.

### Controller level

```ts
import { ApiTags } from '@nestjs/swagger';

@ApiTags('Feature Name')   // single, human-readable group label
@Controller('api/feature')
export class FeatureController { ... }
```

### Every route handler

Apply **all** of the following that are relevant:

| Decorator | When to use |
|-----------|-------------|
| `@ApiOperation({ summary: '...' })` | Always — one sentence describing what the endpoint does |
| `@ApiParam({ name: 'id', type: Number })` | Every `:param` in the path |
| `@ApiBody({ type: ... })` | POST/PATCH/PUT with a request body |
| `@ApiOkResponse` / `@ApiCreatedResponse` / `@ApiAcceptedResponse` | Success response — add `description` |
| `@ApiNotFoundResponse` | When a 404 is possible |
| `@ApiBadRequestResponse` | When validation can fail |
| `@ApiProduces('text/vtt')` | Non-JSON response types |

### Full example

```ts
import {
  ApiCreatedResponse,
  ApiNotFoundResponse,
  ApiOkResponse,
  ApiOperation,
  ApiParam,
  ApiTags,
} from '@nestjs/swagger';

@ApiTags('Recordings')
@Controller('api/recordings')
export class RecordingsController {
  @ApiOperation({ summary: 'Create a recording and enqueue ingest' })
  @ApiCreatedResponse({ description: 'Recording created; ingest job enqueued' })
  @Post()
  create(@Body(new ZodValidationPipe(createRecordingRequestSchema)) body: CreateRecordingRequest) {
    return this.recordingsService.create(body);
  }

  @ApiOperation({ summary: 'Get a recording by ID' })
  @ApiParam({ name: 'id', type: Number })
  @ApiOkResponse({ description: 'Recording object' })
  @ApiNotFoundResponse({ description: 'Recording not found' })
  @Get(':id')
  getById(@Param('id', ParseIntPipe) id: number) {
    return this.recordingsService.getById(id);
  }
}
```

### Rules

- Do **not** skip `@ApiOperation` — it is the primary signal FE devs read.
- Do **not** add `@ApiProperty` to Zod-derived types — they have no class-transformer metadata. Describe the shape with `schema: { example: ... }` inside the response decorator instead.
- The Swagger UI is served at `/docs` (dev only; not exposed behind auth).
